### 7. Evaluation & Rejection of Alternatives
- **Video.js v10**: Evaluated and rejected. Video.js v10 core lacks native YouTube support and requires `videojs-youtube` shims (~30 KB extra) with heavy layout thrash and broken PiP. Plyr v3.7.8 was retained because it includes native, responsive YouTube IFrame support, 48px touch targets, PiP, fullscreen, and respects YouTube brand guidelines.
- **brackets-viewer.js**: Evaluated and rejected (~45 KB). It requires a rigid bracket schema incompatible with LFGOS's 6-school bye structure (Seeds 1 & 2 bye to semifinals; Seeds 3, 4, 5, 6 play quarterfinals). Replaced with a custom 3.8 KB SVG/CSS bracket renderer that directly binds to `feed.fixtures`, displays full school crest shields, and animates winning paths with draw-on stroke animations.
- **Lottie / heavy 3D**: Rejected to keep the core shell under 300 KB and guarantee 60 fps on mid-range mobile devices.
